ENGLISH TRANSLATION
======================================================================

1. Definitions

"Program" means the Project Desktop program: its source code,
documentation, builds (executables), and any changes or additions to them.

"Licensor" means Project (the team that holds the rights to the Program).

"Member" means a person who currently belongs to the Project team and
takes part in the project with the Licensor's knowledge.

2. Permission

For as long as a person is a Member, the Licensor grants that person a
non-transferable, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable permission to:

a) run and use the Program for work on the Project project;
b) read the Program's source code and modify it solely for the needs of
   the Project project.

3. Restrictions

No one, including a Member, may:

a) distribute the Program, its source code or builds, publish them, give
   them to anyone who is not a Member, or make them publicly available;
b) sublicense the Program or transfer rights in it;
c) use the Program or parts of it in other products or projects, or for the
   benefit of third parties;
d) remove or alter copyright notices or this license.

4. Termination

The permission in section 2 lasts only while the person is a Member. It
ends automatically and without notice at the moment the person stops being
a Member, and also upon breach of any term of this license.

After termination, a former Member may not use, modify, or distribute the
Program or parts of it under this license, and must stop using them and
delete any copies of the source code and builds in their possession.

5. Copyright

Copyright in the Program remains with the Licensor. This license grants no
rights other than those expressly stated in section 2. Changes and additions
made to the Program for the Project project are part of the Program unless
the Licensor and the author of the changes agree otherwise in writing.

6. Third-party components

The Program may use third-party libraries and tools (for example ffmpeg,
mpv and others). They remain under their own licenses; this license does
not apply to them and does not override their terms.

7. No warranty

THE PROGRAM IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. NEITHER THE LICENSOR NOR THE AUTHORS ARE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES
ARISING FROM USE OF THE PROGRAM, TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW.
